  <title id="bdlgppriorposterior-title">Samples and two-standard-deviation bands of a Gaussian-process prior and posterior</title>
  <desc id="bdlgppriorposterior-desc">Left: three random functions drawn from a Gaussian-process prior with a squared-exponential kernel, lengthscale 1.6, around a zero mean with a constant band from -2 to 2. Right: after conditioning on seven noisy observations of sin(x) between x = -4 and x = 3.5, the posterior band is narrow at the data, widens slightly in the gap between x = 1.2 and x = 3.5, and grows back toward the prior width away from the data on both sides. Three posterior samples pass close to every observation.</desc>
